1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Caseworkers write notes full of personal data. Cloud AI could turn them into e-mails in seconds — but pasting a note sends a client's name and diagnosis to a server. Boundary splits that job in two.

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:23,000
A sample note about a client: her name, date of birth, address, clinic, panic attacks, a medication, her daughter, her phone and e-mail.

3
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:37,000
Step one runs only on this device: Gemini Nano through Firebase AI Logic, in only-on-device mode. Rules catch the phone, e-mail and date of birth; Nano catches the names and the address.

4
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:44,000
The ledger confirms it: this call ran on the device and sent nothing.

5
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:59,000
This is exactly what the cloud would see: placeholders, each with a short role hint Nano wrote on device — 'the client', 'the daughter' — so the cloud can still write naturally.

6
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:08,000
But Nano missed the clinic, the diagnosis and the medication — they are still in the outgoing text.

7
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:15,000
So the person reviewing adds what the model missed…

8
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:27,000
…and those words are swapped for placeholders before anything leaves. Detection is best effort — that is why this review screen exists.

9
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:37,000
If anything still looks personal — here the phone number, unticked — the send button locks.

10
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:49,000
Right before sending, Nano re-checks the outgoing text on device once more: nothing more found. The ledger now shows two on-device calls, nothing sent.

11
00:01:49,000 --> 00:02:05,000
Step two runs only in the cloud, on placeholder text. It never saw her name. The page puts the real details back locally — no model involved.

12
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:17,000
A prefer-on-device check reads the answer for anything the cloud invented. The ledger shows every call, where it ran, and how many characters left the device.

13
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:26,000
If the on-device model is not available, Boundary stops instead of falling back to the cloud. Boundary — cloud help, with the boundary on your side.
